From ca59438b85cad6840db275a093f39cc410eb9e0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:21:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm: TF_GLM_KV8_INT8=1, int8 codes with two scales a row in
 the 8-bit dsa cache

With --kv-cache fp8 on glm_moe_dsa, TF_GLM_KV8_INT8=1 stores each 576-wide row as int8 codes (the same cache
layout) with two power-of-two scales, 2^ceil(log2(amax / 127)), one for the 512 latent values and one for the 64
rope values (k_pe is not normalized and would set the latent's step): 584 B a token and layer. Codes times scale
stay exact in bf16, so every reader is the bf16 kernel on the dequantized rows (GPU check: bitwise equal, chunks,
decode split, fused, msa sparse and dense). Row RMS error 0.96% on the check's rows against E4M3's 2.67% (the
E4M3 format of patch 0162 failed the 8K agent panel's +0.005 KL gate: +0.037).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQVvNktFCvQrvpNUbqtqBX
